-## What would verify delivery
+The same copy preserves materially different positions. The quoted Shaeffer response disputes a consensus to delay referral or withhold the memo, describes an earlier dissent and requests prompt commissioner circulation. Marcus recalls agreement to defer and restrict circulation, while also expecting commissioners to be briefed on the concerns. Zelikow describes hearing/ethics constraints, recalls proposing immediate referral, and states a preference to decide the issue rather than leave it unresolved. Preserve these positions separately; a single forwarding chain is not independent confirmation of each participant's recollection. Item 03991, p.2 OCR 35–50; p.3 OCR 6–24 and 32–48; p.4 OCR 2–12; p.5 OCR 15–40; p.6 OCR 4–10.
 
-The finding aid documents an archival copy in the vice chair’s hearing materials and the indexed existence of a binder email. The addressee line on the reproduced June 7 memo identifies its intended audience. These observations leave actual dispatch date, which binders contained which version, and which commissioners received or read it unresolved. The reader’s historical document markings and the catalog title are retained as source context. The public HTML does not authenticate the underlying scan, annotations, original authorship field, or signature. The two June memos’ language is preserved with the qualifications in each. The record here does not identify a cause for the wording differences.
